{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015235-disney-traditions-technocracy-nephandi","id":1015235,"title":"Disney: Traditions? Technocracy? Nephandi?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-10T06:46:16-08:00","id":1015235,"title":"Disney: Traditions? Technocracy? Nephandi?","content":"Just coming back from a week at the happiest place on earth. It was obviously great, tons of fun. Part of me feels like DW encourages creativity, love, magic, etc. I also feel like these things are only allowed in certain ways, very controlled. Anyway, anything in canon? Any good headcanon around Disney and their media empire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T08:14:23-08:00","id":1015253,"title":"","content":"Real World? Probably hugely supported by the Traditions, of only morally. It's a place that allows children and adults to be in a place that doesn't really conform to the world outside, someplace that inspires wonder and imagination.<br /> <br /> However, its World of Darkness counterpart would likely, like all things WoD, but a much darker place. Much more obviously a capitalistic money grab, and the illusion is shattered too easily, and too often, for many of the partygoers. In the context of the Ascension War, probably Technocratic or Nephandic, as it serves to both disillusion people from wonder and magic, but also may serve to promote a certain nihilism. However, it doesn't have to be nefarious; it could just be another shitty element of the World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T11:07:32-08:00","id":1015310,"title":"","content":"Walt Disney was almost certainly linked with the Technocracy, if not a Syndicate member himself, then had ties with the Syndicate. The man was a shrewd business man first and formost who always got what he wanted. He may have been an idealist and genuinely believed in the magic of humanity and story, but his was a very sterilised retelling, with style and sentimentality often trumping substance.<br /> <br /> I'd argue that Disneyland's main objective isn't to create a place separate from the real world for people to act as they'd be comfortable, but to sell to people the illusion of &quot;the magic world&quot; while making it abundantly clear that magic can only really exist within these walls. All other forms are in some way lesser or not suitable for decent people. Instead they should prefer the sterilised, plastic, superficial version that Disney provides. Get their children hooked on that, and the &quot;real&quot; stuff will seem like devil-worship or stuffy lectures by comparison.<br /> <br /> In essence they are fulfilling the sleepers desire and interest in the world of magic while making it harmless enough for all to enjoy, and at once define it as pure fiction, and keep it so simple that it actually enforces their sleeper status. After all, It's much harder to unlearn something and then starting anew than it is to learn from scratch.<br /> <br /> It also gives them a chance to trivialise many of the tradition's practices and appropriate their legends.<br /> Pocahontas against the Dreamspeakers<br /> Sword in the Stone against he Verbena<br /> The Sorcerers Apprentice against Hermetics<br /> Treasure Planet against the Etherites<br /> <br /> If the masses accept these traditions as little more than costumes, cartoons, and princesses, then it becomes all the easier for them to default to the technocratic reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 12-10-2016, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T16:55:27-08:00","id":1015411,"title":"","content":"Nefandic, delivering canned wonder by the cost of thousands of lives in its productive process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T17:48:42-08:00","id":1015427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015235-disney-traditions-technocracy-nephandi?p=1015310#post1015310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also gives them a chance to trivialise many of the tradition's practices and appropriate their legends.<br /> Pocahontas against the Dreamspeakers<br /> Sword in the Stone against he Verbena<br /> The Sorcerers Apprentice against Hermetics<br /> Treasure Planet against the Etherites<br /> <br /> If the masses accept these traditions as little more than costumes, cartoons, and princesses, then it becomes all the easier for them to default to the technocratic reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even the more recent Princess films - Tangled and Frozen - enforce a world view about Magic as an in-born trait. Both of the Princesses in those films were born with their powers. It reinforces this idea that &quot;Magic&quot; is something you're born with, rather than it being something that can be learned or studied. This has the effect of keeping such things firmly within the realm of escapist fantasy, dissuading people from entertaining ideas of going out and learning the Art themselves. That is, trying to learn Sorcery Paths (whether that leads to Awakening or no). It makes it so that, even if a person entertains the idea of Magic being real, they don't think of it as being something they, the common person, can do.<br /> <br /> You know what the common person <i>can</i> do? Science. There in lies the trick the Technocracy pulls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T19:33:37-08:00","id":1015480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015235-disney-traditions-technocracy-nephandi?p=1015310#post1015310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It also gives them a chance to trivialise many of the tradition's practices and appropriate their legends.<br /> Pocahontas against the Dreamspeakers<br /> Sword in the Stone against he Verbena<br /> The Sorcerers Apprentice against Hermetics<br /> Treasure Planet against the Etherites<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Mu Lan against the Akashics (&amp; Wu Lung)<br /> The Princess and the Frog against the Ba'ata<br /> Moanna against the Kopa Loei<br /> <br /> Though.... honestly, Tomorrowland and the link with &quot;Meet the Robinsons&quot; seems tremendously pro-Etherite..... <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}